1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,912
Aziz still has a phone number that he has not used since university.

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:08,544
He gave it to the government services portal years ago, and then he forgot it.

3
00:00:08,594 --> 00:00:10,080
MyID did not forget.

4
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:16,136
So when his face passes MyID today, whose phone number is on the record?

5
00:00:16,186 --> 00:00:23,024
In Lesson 17, the verified identity went into the protected class, with the phone number from MyID inside it.

6
00:00:23,074 --> 00:00:28,760
This lesson uses that number for one job: the phone check, the last step before level two.

7
00:00:28,810 --> 00:00:32,632
Why is a face not enough?

8
00:00:32,682 --> 00:00:39,952
Level two means two things at once: MyID proved the person, and the phone number of the account belongs to that person.

9
00:00:40,002 --> 00:00:42,016
A face proves who holds the phone.

10
00:00:42,066 --> 00:00:44,488
It does not prove that the number is his.

11
00:00:44,538 --> 00:00:50,368
Picture a man who gets a SIM card with a stranger's number, and passes MyID with his own face.

12
00:00:50,418 --> 00:00:54,856
Without a phone check, he would get level two on a number that belongs to somebody else.

13
00:00:54,906 --> 00:00:59,080
So, after Aziz confirms his data, the phone check starts.

14
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:03,640
It runs only in a step-up, and a refresh does not repeat it.

15
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:12,544
Step one: the platform sends TAF a face confirmation, with Aziz's personal identification number and his verified phone number.

16
00:01:12,594 --> 00:01:17,296
The app never sees the personal identification number, because the platform sends it.

17
00:01:17,346 --> 00:01:24,496
Step two: the platform compares Aziz's verified number with the number from MyID, as full international numbers.

18
00:01:24,546 --> 00:01:26,944
The same number gives the status Confirmed.

19
00:01:26,994 --> 00:01:31,864
But Aziz's numbers differ: the MyID one is his old university number.

20
00:01:31,914 --> 00:01:40,264
Step three: the platform asks TAF a second question: does this phone number belong to this personal identification number?

21
00:01:40,314 --> 00:01:44,872
TAF compares the number with the personal identification number from step one.

22
00:01:44,922 --> 00:01:46,744
Owner gives Confirmed.

23
00:01:46,794 --> 00:01:52,528
Not owner, account not found, or no answer from TAF gives Processing.

24
00:01:52,578 --> 00:01:55,384
Today, TAF says owner.

25
00:01:55,434 --> 00:01:59,680
Aziz's status is Confirmed, and three things happen together.

26
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:02,704
He is at level two, in every app of the bank.

27
00:02:02,754 --> 00:02:07,648
His phone becomes a trusted device, and he gets a new access grant with level two.

28
00:02:07,698 --> 00:02:10,792
And linking starts, which the next lesson explains.

29
00:02:10,842 --> 00:02:14,224
Now suppose that TAF had said: not owner.

30
00:02:14,274 --> 00:02:16,552
Aziz's status would be Processing.

31
00:02:16,602 --> 00:02:20,584
He would stay at level one, and the app would show him the word Processing.

32
00:02:20,634 --> 00:02:25,672
The platform opens a phone review, and sends an event to the bank's antifraud system.

33
00:02:25,722 --> 00:02:35,800
The review shows an operator his phone number, his personal identification number masked, the MyID number masked except the last four digits, the time, the device and the app.

34
00:02:35,850 --> 00:02:37,672
There is no timer.

35
00:02:37,722 --> 00:02:41,056
Aziz stays at level one until a person decides.

36
00:02:41,106 --> 00:02:44,560
I think Processing is the bravest state in this design.

37
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:49,360
The platform admits that it does not know, and it waits for a human instead of a guess.

38
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:53,272
The operator approves or rejects, and must write a reason.

39
00:02:53,322 --> 00:02:58,648
Approval does what Confirmed did: level two, a trusted device, and linking.

40
00:02:58,698 --> 00:03:02,752
Rejection keeps Aziz at level one, with the status Rejected.

41
00:03:02,802 --> 00:03:07,024
Both send him a security notification, and both go to the audit trail.

42
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:11,416
And the review list in the admin panel is the only alert that operators get.

43
00:03:11,466 --> 00:03:14,152
Back to the real Aziz, who is confirmed.

44
00:03:14,202 --> 00:03:17,440
His record now has a short history next to the number.

45
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:21,424
Each check of the number is kept, with the provider, the app and the time.

46
00:03:21,474 --> 00:03:26,488
A code from the bank's SMS service, in the marketplace, last March.

47
00:03:26,538 --> 00:03:30,808
A TAF check, in the mobile bank, at registration.

48
00:03:30,858 --> 00:03:33,568
A MyID check, in the mobile bank, today.

49
00:03:33,618 --> 00:03:38,680
So the bank can always answer one question: how do we know that this number is Aziz's?

50
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:50,464
To recap: a face confirmation to TAF, then the number from MyID, then TAF ownership, then a person; Confirmed gives level two, and Processing waits for a review.

51
00:03:50,514 --> 00:03:55,696
Aziz is confirmed, and the platform knows his personal identification number.

52
00:03:55,746 --> 00:04:00,736
But is he already a customer of the bank, with accounts and cards somewhere in its records?

53
00:04:00,786 --> 00:04:04,864
And how does the platform find him there, without ever trusting a phone number?

54
00:04:04,914 --> 00:04:06,736
Next: linking.
